---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy" description="Privacy information for Dealer AI Plugins and its skills-only plugin packages.">
  <article class="content-page">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> Privacy</div>
    <h1>Transparent by design.</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Dealer AI Plugins distributes static, skills-only packages. This website does not require an account and the plugins do not include a hosted MCP server, authentication flow, tracking SDK, or database operated by Dealer AI Plugins.</p>
      <h2>Data we collect</h2>
      <p>Dealer Growth Hackers does not collect the prompts, files, dealership records, customer records, generated answers, or connected-account data that you use with an installed plugin. The marketplace does not offer user accounts, forms, comments, advertising profiles, or email subscriptions.</p>
      <h2>Purpose and use</h2>
      <p>The marketplace serves public pages and downloadable plugin packages. The packages provide instructions that run inside the AI product where you install them. Dealer Growth Hackers does not receive or use the content of those interactions.</p>
      <h2>Service providers and recipients</h2>
      <p>Cloudflare hosts the marketplace and may process ordinary web-delivery information such as IP addresses, request headers, timestamps, and requested URLs for security, reliability, and delivery. GitHub hosts the public source repository and issue tracker. If you follow an external link or use a connected tool, that service processes information under its own privacy policy.</p>
      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>Dealer Growth Hackers does not retain plugin prompts, uploaded files, generated answers, or dealership data because it does not receive them. Cloudflare and GitHub retain operational information according to their own published policies and account settings.</p>
      <h2>Your choices and controls</h2>
      <p>You may use the public pages without creating an account, choose whether to download or install a plugin, remove an installed plugin at any time, and avoid sending personal or confidential information to an AI product or connected tool. Requests about this policy can be submitted through the public support channel.</p>
      <h2>Information you provide elsewhere</h2>
      <p>Information you provide while using an installed plugin is handled by the AI product and any tools you choose to connect. Do not provide passwords, API keys, payment-card information, government identifiers, health information, or customer personal information unless the connected product and your dealership policies explicitly permit it.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions, <a href="https://github.com/arielcoro/dealer-ai-plugins/issues">open an issue in the public repository</a>. Do not include personal, confidential, or dealership customer information in a public issue.</p>
      <p>Last updated: October 1, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
